cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RiceBaCI-GEE: Decoupling Cyclone-Induced Saline Inundation from Agronomic Flooding in Sentinel-1/2 Rice Phenology Retrieval"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: Panda
    given-names: Subranab
    affiliation: "PhD Researcher, Agricultural Meteorology, Bhubaneswar, Odisha, India"
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/[your-handle]/RiceBaCI-GEE"
abstract: >
  RiceBaCI-GEE is an open Google Earth Engine toolkit that distinguishes cyclone-induced
  saline inundation from normal agronomic transplanting flooding in Sentinel-1/2 rice
  time-series, and uses this distinction to recover unbiased phenological dates (SOS,
  POS, EOS) for coastal Odisha Kharif rice from 2017 to 2024. The framework uses a
  Before-After-Control-Impact (BACI) design with three named tropical cyclones (Fani
  2019, Amphan 2020, Yaas 2021) as natural experiments.
keywords:
  - Sentinel-1
  - Sentinel-2
  - rice phenology
  - tropical cyclone
  - SAR-optical fusion
  - Google Earth Engine
  - BACI design
  - coastal Odisha
  - agricultural meteorology
date-released: "2026-05-01"
version: "0.1.0"
